     "ward",
     "councillor",
     "mayor"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "A big city has a Municipal Corporation headed by a Mayor. The city is divided into wards and each ward elects a councillor.\nWard committees bring people close to the corporation so that residents can raise problems like water supply and garbage. This is participatory democracy.\nMunicipal corporations have a long history: the first in India was in Madras in 1688."
    }
   },
